  "goodToKnow": "Die Infektionskrankheit is an infectious disease. Under Germany's Infektionsschutzgesetz, many are meldepflichtig (notifiable) to the Gesundheitsamt, and the Robert Koch-Institut, named after the German founder of bacteriology, monitors them. Since March 2020, the Masernschutzgesetz requires proof of measles vaccination for children in Kitas and schools. Plural: die Infektionskrankheiten."
